    "modelText": "{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"week07.student-model/v1\",\n  \"id\": \"week07-student-model\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"slots\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"controls.demand\",\n      \"expressions\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"requiredMoment\",\n          \"expression\": \"inertia*target_acceleration-competing_moment\",\n          \"unit\": \"N*m\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"controls.effectiveness\",\n      \"expressions\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"dynamicPressure\",\n          \"expression\": \"0.5*density *V*V\",\n          \"unit\": \"Pa\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"deltaCm\",\n          \"expression\": \"ms / q_inf*S*chord_length\",\n          \"unit\": \"1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"deltaMoment\",\n          \"expression\": \"deltaCm*q_inf*S*chord_length\",\n          \"unit\": \"N*m\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}",
    "modelHash": "fnv1a-7cf025dc",
    "fields": {
      "question": {
        "suppliedBy": "instructor",
        "locked": true,
        "text": "Calculate required control moment, elevator moment, and the change with airspeed. Explain whether the nominal response meets +0.12 rad/s²."
      },
      "system": {
        "suppliedBy": "instructor",
        "locked": true,
        "text": "Illustrative planar pitch model. Aircraft geometry, integration, force conversion and constraints are supplied."
      },
      "representation": {
        "suppliedBy": "instructor",
        "locked": true,
        "text": "Body axes forward/right/down. Positive pitch moment nose-up. Positive Fz downward. Positive elevator trailing edge down. Reference/CG X=0 m; tail X=-3 m."
      },
      "physics": {
        "suppliedBy": "student",
        "locked": false,
        "text": "Because the plane rotates along the CG, as the tail drops, the nose will rise, essentially rotating in the same direction of the tail."
      },
      "assumptions": {
        "suppliedBy": "student",
        "locked": false,
        "text": "Assumption: rudder and ailerons will not be used, constraining the motion to one axis\nWhat could invalidate it: external wind forcing trim or generating unwanted plane movement (roll or yaw)"
      },
      "inputs": {
        "suppliedBy": "instructor",
        "locked": true,
        "text": "Iy=5000 kg·m²; target=+0.12 rad/s²; competing=-750 N-m; density=1.225 kg/m³; V=40 m/s; S=16 m²; chord=1.5 m; Cmδ=-0.8/rad; elevator=-5°. Inputs are illustrative, not calibrated."
      },
      "model": {
        "suppliedBy": "student",
        "locked": false,
        "text": "demand: control moment + competing moment = inertia × target acceleration.\ndynamic-pressure: 0.5 × density × V^2\ncoefficient equations: deltaCm = ms / q∞ × S × chord length\nmoment equations: deltaM = deltaCm × q∞ ×  S × chord length"
      },
      "prediction": {
        "suppliedBy": "student",
        "locked": false,
        "text": "Elevator sign should be positive\n\nHalving the airspeed should reduce the moment of the elevator by a factor 4.\n\nTail pitches down, noise pitches up"
      },
      "execution": {
        "suppliedBy": "automatic",
        "locked": false,
        "text": ""
      },
      "verification": {
        "suppliedBy": "student",
        "locked": false,
        "text": "0.5*1.225*40*40 = 980 Pa"
      },
